[{"text":"DiracGammaExpand[exp] expands Dirac matrices contracted to linear combinations of \\(4\\)-vectors. All DiracGamma[Momentum[a+b+ ...]] will be expanded to DiracGamma[Momentum[a]] + DiracGamma[Momentum[b]] + DiracGamma[Momentum[...]] .","anchor":"diracgammaexpand"},{"text":"Overview, DiracGamma, DiracGammaCombine, DiracSimplify, DiracTrick.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"GS[q] . GS[p - q] ex = DiracGammaExpand[%]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}-\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex // StandardForm (*DiracGamma[Momentum[q]] . (DiracGamma[Momentum[p]] - DiracGamma[Momentum[q]])*)","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGammaExpand rewrites \\gamma^{\\mu } (p-q)_{\\mu } as \\gamma^{mu } p_{mu } - \\gamma^{\\mu } q_{\\mu }.","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The inverse operation is DiracGammaCombine.","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GS[q] . (GS[p] - GS[q]) ex = DiracGammaCombine[%]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}-\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"ex // StandardForm (*DiracGamma[Momentum[q]] . DiracGamma[Momentum[p - q]]*)","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"It is possible to perform the expansions only on Dirac matrices contracted with particular momenta.","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"c1 GAD[\\[Mu]] . (GSD[p1 + p2] + m) . GAD[\\[Nu]] + c2 GAD[\\[Mu]] . (GSD[q1 + q2] + m) . GAD[\\[Nu]] DiracGammaExpand[%, Momentum -> {q1}]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{c1} \\gamma ^{\\mu }.(m+\\gamma \\cdot (\\text{p1}+\\text{p2})).\\gamma ^{\\nu }+\\text{c2} \\gamma ^{\\mu }.(m+\\gamma \\cdot (\\text{q1}+\\text{q2})).\\gamma ^{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{c1} \\gamma ^{\\mu }.(m+\\gamma \\cdot (\\text{p1}+\\text{p2})).\\gamma ^{\\nu }+\\text{c2} \\gamma ^{\\mu }.(m+\\gamma \\cdot \\;\\text{q1}+\\gamma \\cdot \\;\\text{q2}).\\gamma ^{\\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"If the input expression contains DiracSigma, DiracGammaExpand will expand Feynman slashes inside DiracSigma and call DiracSigmaExpand.","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSigma[GSD[p + q], GSD[r]] DiracGammaExpand[%]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\sigma ^{p+qr}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\sigma ^{pr}+\\sigma ^{qr}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"The call to DiracSigmaExpand can be inhibited by disabling the corresponding option.","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracGammaExpand[DiracSigma[GSD[p + q], GSD[r]], DiracSigmaExpand -> False]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{DiracSigma}(\\gamma \\cdot p+\\gamma \\cdot q,\\gamma \\cdot r)\\]","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Use DiracSimplify for noncommutative expansions with the corresponding simplifications.","anchor":"cb7-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DiracSimplify[GS[q] . (GS[p - q])]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right)-\\overline{q}^2\\]","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"If simplifications are not required, you may also combine DiracGammaExpand with DotSimplify.","anchor":"cb8-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"DotSimplify[DiracGammaExpand[GS[q] . (GS[p - q])]]","anchor":"cb9","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\right)-\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right).\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb9-1","section":"Examples"}]